Title: "Adjective"
Id: "a7cb8bbd-b930-4dc3-a6f4-0ddbdfd69eec"

Text: "`adjective:` is the required documented text item for `Refines:` entries.

```mlg-fragment
Documented:
. adjective: \"injective\"
```

When a refined type is rendered, the adjective is placed before the base type's rendered name. A single refinement such as `\(a)::type` renders as `<a> <type>`, while `\(a, b, c)::type` renders as `(<a>, <b>, and <c>) <type>`.

Refined **specification-infix** forms use the opposite order: the rendered base relation comes first, followed by the refinements in parentheses, so `X \:(a, b, c)::relation:/ Y` renders as `<X relation Y> (<a>, <b>, and <c>)`. An explicit `written:` template overrides either default.

`Refines:` may also contain `written:`, but it may not contain `called:`. The adjective supplies the prose name that would otherwise be carried by `called:`."
Id: "de66f7d9-1f4a-416b-9308-e08651b503b5"
